PRE-TABLE AMENDMENT, PART 6b -- its own file, written AFTER part 6 and BEFORE part 6b (its
mtime against part6/driver.log and part6b/driver.log is the order witness; not edited after).

SECTION 13 -- a prediction that FAILED in the safe direction, and the vacuous rows it exposed.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Section 12 predicted M_W4FALL_ALL -> 137/159 (22 red).  MEASURED (part6/driver.log): 139/159,
twenty red.  `rb8 t2ctl' and `rb8 t2icr' stayed GREEN under the fall-through -- the landed
8-byte lane 0x33 equals the preset through each arm's mask: TxCTL (0x03 & 0xfc) | (0x33 & 3)
= 0x03; TxICR (0x13 & ~0x17) | (0x33 & 0x17) = 0x13.  Section 12 enumerated the landed lanes
for len 4 ("TxICR 0x15") and did not enumerate them for len 8.  Two readback rows were vacuous
BY VALUE CHOICE: the mutant landed the write and the row could not see it.  L1, pre-ship
construction: the value is changed, not the rows.
THE RULE THIS PINS: a readback row's value is chosen per ARM, against that arm's mask, so that
the landed lane differs from the preset; enumerate the lane for EVERY width the row drives.
Landed lanes for 0x..44 under the fall-through: GENCTL 0x44 (preset 0x82), VECBASE 0x40 (0x50),
TxCTL 0x00 (0x03), TxICR 0x04 (0x13), SCCICR 0x04 (0x1f), SCCTX 0x44 (0x1f), SCCRX 0x44 (0x1f),
SCSIICR 0x44 (0x1f), MASK 0x44 (0x12) -- all differ.
PREDICTIONS for part 6b (one mutant plus BASE, on the corrected instrument):
    BASE            159/159
    M_W4FALL_ALL    137/159  all nine rb4, all nine rb8, pscale noig4/8, ipl noig4/8 (22 red)
TRANSFER: the part-6 scores of M_NOWRITECHK_VECBASE (158), M_NOWRITECHK_GENCTL (157) and the two
M_PENDT mutants stand -- the only rows changed carry a different declined value, and a declined
write's readback is the preset whatever the value; adding a kill cannot un-kill a mutant.
